# Wolseley Hornet (Mini-based) two-door saloon, 1961-1969.
#
# The Mini-based Hornet: the long-wheelbase Mini shell with the Wolseley
# grille, the illuminated badge and the boot. The Mk II and Mk III noses are
# within the pack; the model represents the range.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wolseley_Hornet_(1961)
#
# Dimensions 3.310 x 1.397 x 1.346 m, wheelbase 2.036 m.
#
# Shape reference: NO true side profile exists. Image 1 is a front
# three-quarter; the proportional Mini shell and the Wolseley grille and
# badge govern. The limitation is recorded.
#
# Colours: grade (c); the notes record the period palette. Black, white, red
# and blue are used. Weights 9, 8, 7, 6, total 30, provisional.
#
# Speed 130 km/h. Comfort 60/270, on the line 180 + 1.5 x 60: the Mini
# cabin with a little more rear room. Classes 1,2.
# Dates are road presence: 1961 intro, retires staggered 1983-1986.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/wolseley-hornet-mini.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/wolseley-hornet-mini.dae. References:
# citycars/references/wolseley-hornet-mini/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: there is no true side or rear view, so the profile and
# extended boot are inferred. The front corners and grille are too angular. At
# 128 px the Mini shell with the Wolseley grille and badge reads as a Hornet.


obj=citycar
name=WolseleyHornetMini(Black)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=9
intro_year=1961
intro_month=10
retire_year=1986
retire_month=6
speed=130
class=1,2
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=60
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=270

Image[E]=./images/wolseley-hornet-mini-black_E.0.0,-33,14
Image[SE]=./images/wolseley-hornet-mini-black_SE.0.0,-13,0
